rustic for Debian
-----------------

This package ships no configuration file. rustic takes its options from TOML
profiles, which it looks for in ~/.config/rustic/ and in the global directory
/etc/rustic/.

Upstream's profiles are installed as examples, with the specification that
describes them:

  /usr/share/doc/rustic/examples/

simple.toml is the one to start from; full.toml documents every option.

Nothing is installed into /etc/rustic/: a profile shipped there would be a dpkg
conffile, tracked and prompted about on every upgrade that changed it. A
profile you create there is yours and dpkg will not touch it.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
